        "duration": 1882.093333,
        "source_notes": "-------------------------\r\nPHiSH\r\n-------------------------\r\n09/14/2000\r\nDarien Lake\r\nDarien, NY\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nSOURCE:\r\n-------------------------\r\nNeumann u89i (Cardiod, 80Hz roll off, DFC Taper's Section)>\r\nMackie 1202 VLS>\r\nTascam DA-P1 @ 48kHz>\r\nSony PCM-M1>\r\nMontego II S/PDIF>\r\nCool Edit 2000 @ 44.1kHz/CDWav>\r\n.WAV/.SHN\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nRECORDED BY:\r\n-------------------------\r\nBryan Austin\r\nbaustin@clemson.edu\r\n\r\nDave Schall\r\npqxp@umich.edu\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nCONVERSION BY:\r\n-------------------------\r\nBryan Austin\r\nbaustin@clemson.edu\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nDISC 1 (62:59)\r\n-------------------------\r\nSET 1\r\n1.  Crowd\r\n2.  PYITE\r\n3.  Reba\r\n4.  Albuquerque\r\n5.  Carini\r\n6.  Oh Kee Pa Ceremony>\r\n7.  Suzie Greenberg\r\n8.  Suzie Greenberg Jam\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nDISC 2 (46:44)\r\n-------------------------\r\nSET 2a\r\n1.  Crowd\r\n2.  Drowned\r\n3.  Cross Eyed and Painless\r\n4.  Dog Faced Boy\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nDISC 3 (38:48)\r\n-------------------------\r\nSET 2b\r\n1.  Prince Caspian\r\n2.  Loving Cup\r\n\r\nEncore\r\n3.  Driver\r\n4.  The Inlaw Josie Wales\r\n5.  Sample in a Jar\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nNOTE:\r\n-------------------------\r\nI'd prefer that the opening crowd noises are not removed,\r\nbut I could honestly care less. I feel it helps recreate\r\nthe experience. Also, if this source is converted to any\r\nother format(ie- .MP3, .RA,...), please include this file\r\nand add any changes to the source.\r\nThanx & Enjoy!\r\n-Bryan\r\n\r\nSend any questions or comments to:\r\nbaustin@clemson.edu",
